{"name":"Swiss Livery","hex":"#c6c3b4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"swiss","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To prepare (meat, fabric, etc.) by rolling or pounding in order to soften it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swiss"},{"term":"livery","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any distinctive identifying uniform worn by a group, such as the uniform worn by chauffeurs and male servants.","The whole body of liverymen, members of livery companies."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To clothe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/livery"}],"entries":[{"title":"Livery","blocks":[{"text":"A livery is an identifying design, such as a uniform, ornament, symbol, or insignia that designates ownership or affiliation, often found on an individual or vehicle. Livery often includes elements of the heraldry relating to the individual or corporate body featured in the livery. Alternatively, some kind of a personal emblem or badge, or a distinctive colour, is featured."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Yeomen_of_the_Guard.JPG/330px-Yeomen_of_the_Guard.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Livery"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Auguste_Serrure_A_distraction_from_chores.jpg/500px-Auguste_Serrure_A_distraction_from_chores.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Auguste_Serrure_A_distraction_from_chores.jpg/500px-Auguste_Serrure_A_distraction_from_chores.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Footman c. 1780 in braided livery","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAuguste_Serrure_A_distraction_from_chores.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/State_Opening_of_Parliam